## Scope and estimands

The work contains six distinct estimands that should have separate datasets and metrics:

1. persistent neuron localization and identity;
2. trace extraction conditional on an ROI;
3. activation/event inference conditional on a trace;
4. left/right/neutral intent before movement onset;
5. next neural/behavioral state conditional on current state and stimulation action;
6. a constrained policy that selects an action for a desired outcome.

Success at an upstream estimand is necessary but not sufficient downstream. In particular, passive intent prediction is not a causal stimulation model.
